  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is zero information about whether multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation, or learned encoders (scGPT, scVI) provide any benefit over a simple single-modality model. The most critical unknown is the performance ceiling of each individual modality. 2) What this tests: config_015 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet50, no aggregation, no fusion) is the simplest possible image-based classifier. It establishes a clean performance baseline for the morphology modality alone, free from confounding by RNA fusion, profile aggregation, or encoder complexity. 3) Why it is the best first use of budget: Before investing in complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations, we need a reference point. A simple, well-understood baseline (ResNet50 on single images) is the most interpretable anchor: any future multimodal or multiprofile experiment can be directly compared to it to determine whether added complexity is justified. It also reduces uncertainty about the image modality's standalone contribution, which is essential for interpreting all subsequent fusion and aggregation experiments."
